(6935078, 1044666, 141319, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Art Roflmao:</b></div><hr/><i> Hard to hear me with my foot in my mouth, but, CONGRATS! ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not at all :-). Thank you for your original comment. Clearly the sky wasn''t "strong" enough to show what I wanted it to show. I thought your comment was most useful, honestly. <br/>I did think it should have been darker actually, but that was the best I could get it to without loosing other stuff. Not sure if there are stronger polarising filters? When I bought mine they just gave me the one I now have. Never asked a question, so I assumed that is what there is. Will check that out.</td>', 'Originally posted by Art Roflmao: Hard to hear me with my foot in my mouth, but, CONGRATS! ;-)   Not at all :-). Thank you for your original comment. Clearly the sky wasn''t "strong" enough to show what I wanted it to show. I thought your comment was most useful, honestly. I did think it should have been darker actually, but that was the best I could get it to without loosing other stuff. Not sure if there are stronger polarising filters? When I bought mine they just gave me the one I now have. Never asked a question, so I assumed that is what there is. Will check that out.', '2012-12-17 02:25:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6935096, 1044402, 28742, '<td valign="top">I gave it a 5 - there seems to be too much of a visual contrast between the smooth, blurred water and the sharp, detailed pier for my liking. It''s like the pier was masked off and then the water was heavily Gaussian blurred - even though I am sure that''s not the case. Just my two cents.</td>', 'I gave it a 5 - there seems to be too much of a visual contrast between the smooth, blurred water and the sharp, detailed pier for my liking. It''s like the pier was masked off and then the water was heavily Gaussian blurred - even though I am sure that''s not the case. Just my two cents.', '2012-12-17 02:42:44.000000', NULL, 0),
